  "solution": "Let the roots be \\(r\\) and \\(s\\).\n\nFor the quadratic \\(3x^2+4x-9=0\\):\n\n\\[\nr+s = -\\frac{4}{3}, \\qquad rs = \\frac{-9}{3}=-3\n\\]\n\nWe want:\n\n\\[\nr^2+s^2\n\\]\n\nUsing the identity:\n\n\\[\nr^2+s^2=(r+s)^2-2rs\n\\]\n\nSubstitute:\n\n\\[\nr^2+s^2=\\left(-\\frac{4}{3}\\right)^2-2(-3)\n\\]\n\n\\[\n=\\frac{16}{9}+6\n\\]\n\n\\[\n=\\frac{16}{9}+\\frac{54}{9}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n=\\frac{70}{9}\n\\]\n\nThe answer is \\(\\frac{70}{9}\\).",
